Package: lcd
Type: Package
Title: Learn Chain Graphs via Decomposition
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
  person("Zongming", "Ma", role = "aut"),
  person("Xiangrui", "Meng", role = "aut"),
  person(
    "Vincent",
    "Guillemot", 
    role = "cre",
    email = "contact@vincentguillemot.fr"))
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
Imports: MASS, ggm, igraph, methods, stats
Description: Implements constraint-based algorithms for learning chain graphs,
        including Bayesian networks and Markov networks, from continuous or
        discrete data. Following Ma et al. (2008)
        <https://jmlr.org/papers/v9/ma08a.html>, it decomposes the learning
        problem into smaller subproblems and provides algorithms for skeleton
        recovery and edge orientation, without requiring complete separators.
        The package also provides tools for graph manipulation, conditional
        independence testing, and sampling from chain-graph models.
License: GPL (>= 2)
